// Frosted-glass blur for trollshell's translucent chrome surfaces.
//
// Requires niri >= 26.04 (the `ext-background-effect` protocol / layer-rule
// `background-effect` block). niri does NOT support `include`, so merge each
// `layer-rule { }` block below into ~/.config/niri/config.kdl by hand
// (see the "Frosted-glass blur" section in etc/niri/README.md).
//
// IMPORTANT: blur only shows THROUGH a translucent surface. These rules are
// paired with `@shell_background` carrying an alpha < 1 in
// assets/trollshell/style.css — over an opaque surface the blur is invisible.
//
// CLIENT-SIDE REGION SCOPING (niri >= 26.04): these layer-rules frost the WHOLE
// surface geometry, not the painted content. trollshell additionally scopes the
// frost to the visible card via ext-background-effect-v1 `set_blur_region` (the
// `hytte-blur` crate, #192/#193) — so the sidebar/drawer frost hugs the card and
// no strip lingers when closed. KEEP these blocks — they are REQUIRED, not just
// a niri < 26.04 fallback: (1) they ENABLE blur per namespace (the client region
// only NARROWS it); (2) `xray false` on the sidebar/drawer is layer-rule-only —
// the client `set_blur_region` protocol forces `xray true`, so "protocol-only /
// drop blur.kdl" is NOT viable for the overlays. On niri < 26.04 the client
// scoping is a graceful no-op and the layer-rule blur is the (un-scoped)
// fallback — keep the blocks merged.
//
// `match namespace=` is a regex matched anywhere in the surface namespace:
//   hytte-bar-{edge}    -> the bar              (crates/hytte-ui/src/bar.rs:106)
//   hytte-sidebar-{id}  -> the pushable sidebar (overlays/sidebar.rs:218)
//   hytte-modal-{id}    -> the slide-out drawer (modal.rs:449)
//
// DELIBERATELY NOT BLURRED (fullscreen surfaces — blurring them frosts the
// WHOLE screen):
//   hytte-frame         -> fullscreen click-through frame overlay
//   hytte-popup-catcher -> invisible fullscreen dismiss catcher
//   hytte-modal         -> the slide-out drawer (DROPPED FOR NOW — curved card
//                          edges shimmer under a rectangles-only blur region;
//                          see the commented-out rule below)
//
// `xray true` frosts the wallpaper only (cheap, computed once); `xray false`
// frosts the actual content behind the surface (pricier; niri recomputes on
// movement). The BAR sits over wallpaper — `xray true` is correct and cheap,
// nothing occludes it. The SIDEBAR and DRAWER overlay the window stack:
// `xray true` would frost only the occluded wallpaper and leave windows sharp
// — no visible frost. `xray false` frosts the actual window content behind
// them. Trade-off: a touch brighter/off-colour next to the bar, but it's the
// only way the overlay frost shows over windows.

layer-rule {
    match namespace="hytte-bar"
    // Full-width flush strip — no rounding.
    geometry-corner-radius 0
    background-effect {
        blur true
        xray true
    }
}

layer-rule {
    match namespace="hytte-sidebar"
    // Flush left panel; the frame overlay paints the rounded inner corner.
    // xray false: the sidebar overlays the window stack, so xray true would
    // frost only the occluded wallpaper and leave windows sharp — no visible
    // frost. xray false frosts the actual window content behind the sidebar.
    geometry-corner-radius 0
    background-effect {
        blur true
        xray false
    }
}

// DROPPED FOR NOW (hytte-modal / the slide-out drawer): the drawer card is a
// *curved* silhouette — concave top wings sweeping up to the bar + convex bottom
// corners — and a client `set_blur_region` is rectangles-only, so the frost
// can't hug those edges (it shimmers along them and during the reveal slide).
// Until the curved-edge frost is solved, the drawer is unblurred. The shell now
// hands niri an EMPTY blur region on each drawer map (modal.rs `wire_blur_attach`),
// which suppresses this rule even while it stays merged — so removing it from the
// live config is optional. To drop the frost the clean way, also delete this block
// from ~/.config/niri/config.kdl and reload niri. Re-enable: un-comment below and
// restore the card-scoping in modal.rs (git revert the drop commit).
//
// layer-rule {
//     match namespace="hytte-modal"
//     geometry-corner-radius 14
//     background-effect {
//         blur true
//         xray false
//     }
// }
